course: dictionary
lesson: 14688
title: Pretence and pretending
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pretence is when you act as if something is true when it is not. «Sam closed his eyes and lay very still. It was a pretence: he was not asleep, he just wanted to avoid the washing up.» The clue is the words "he was not asleep".
explain: Pretence is also part of play. «The girls played shops with pretend money.» This is make-believe, and it is a normal, happy part of childhood. The difference from a trick is that everyone knows it is pretend.
explain: Sometimes a pretence hides the real reason for doing something. «Under the pretence of helping, the boy took the cake.» The helping was a false reason, and the real reason was hidden. When you meet pretence in a story, ask what the character is really feeling or planning.
explain: "Make no pretence" means not even trying to look like something. «He made no pretence of liking the gift.» The words tell you he clearly did not like it.
fact: Pretence is a noun: a pretence, some pretences.
fact: «Pretence» means acting as if something is true when it is not.
fact: «Under the pretence of» means using a false reason to hide the real one.
fact: «Make no pretence» means not even trying to look like something you are not.
fact: In American English the spelling is pretense.
exercise: «She made a pretence of being happy at the party, but she was really very sad.» What is a pretence here? | A party game with prizes | A loud noise made by a crowd | Being happy for real | *Acting as if something is true when it is not
exercise: «They played pirates with pretend swords all afternoon.» What kind of pretence is this? | A false reason to hide the truth | A real, sharp weapon | *Make-believe play | Making no effort at all
exercise: «He made no pretence of liking the gift.» What does made no pretence mean? | He hid the gift under his bed | *He did not even try to look as if he liked it | He gave it back straight away | He pretended to love it very much
test: Mum says, «Never let a stranger in who visits under false pretences.» What does false pretences mean? | Playing a fun game with friends | *Using a false reason to trick people | Telling a true story about the weather | Being very quiet and shy
test: Sia asks, «Is pretend play bad?» What is the best answer? | No, but only after you are twelve | Yes, you must never play pretend | *No, make-believe is a normal, healthy part of play | Yes, pretending is always lying
exam: «Tom's smile was a pretence; his eyes filled with tears when no one was looking.» What does the pretence show? | *He was hiding his real feelings | He was really happy and full of fun | He had made a promise to his mum | He was playing a make-believe game with friends
